github.com/raftseg/raft  (a separate module, compiled into products)
    raftseg requires this first-party module, a fork of etcd raft v3.6.0
    (Apache License 2.0, copyright The etcd Authors). It carries its own
    LICENSE and NOTICE, which products that compile it in must include;
    its FORK.md lists every change from upstream, and upstream.json the
    upstream release and the upstream commits cherry-picked since.

seglog/  (compiled into products)
    Written by the raftseg authors. Its segment files use the record format
    of LevelDB's log files, as implemented by Pebble
    (github.com/cockroachdb/pebble, BSD-3-Clause): 32 KiB blocks of chunks,
    each with a masked CRC-32C. seglog implements the format itself and
    includes no LevelDB or Pebble code. seglog/testdata/wire_golden.json and
    wire_edge.bin.gz are streams written by Pebble's record.Writer
    (github.com/cockroachdb/pebble/v2 v2.1.7) for the compatibility tests;
    seglog/testdata/genwire.go.txt is the program that wrote them.

internal/datadriven/  (used by tests only; not compiled into products)
    Origin:     github.com/cockroachdb/datadriven
                v1.0.3-0.20250407164829-2945557346d5
    Copyright:  The Cockroach Authors
    License:    internal/datadriven/LICENSE
    Changes:    The github.com/pmezard/go-difflib dependency was replaced
                by diff.go, which uses only the standard library.

internal/testutil/  (used by tests only; not compiled into products)
    Written by the raftseg authors. Its API and failure behaviour follow
    github.com/stretchr/testify (MIT), so that the upstream raft tests run
    unchanged. No testify code is included.
    testdata/testifycompat compares the two directly.
